  "question": {
    "text": "A storage tower supplies water, as shown in the figure. If&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is the atmospheric pressure<br />\r<br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>= height of water level,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g&nbsp;</mi></math>= acceleration due to gravity,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo></math> density and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>= velocity of flow in the horizontal pipe at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>, then the pressure at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;is -<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0076_ea0310ceda3e.png\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 270px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
